It is early in the morning.
Outside, it is still dark.
At half past six, my phone rings.
That is my alarm.
I open my eyes.
I wake up.
I am still a little tired.
The bed is warm and cozy.
But today is a workday.
I do not stay in bed.
I get up right away.
The room is cool.
I pick up my phone.
I turn off the alarm.
Then I walk into the bathroom.
I turn on the light.
My day begins.
